# Backend aside (`apps/backend-adonis`)

**Legacy AdonisJS 7 tree** kept as a reference during the Hono migration. Active API is `apps/backend` (Hono) — see `hono-backend` rule.

AdonisJS 7 API app. **Follow [AdonisJS official folder structure](https://docs.adonisjs.com/guides/getting-started/folder-structure) and Ace naming generators**.

SSOT for layout/names: Adonis docs + `node ace make:*`. Placement vs monorepo packages: `layering` + `structure` (Adonis `app/**` is a **framework tree** exception to flat-by-default).

## Official directory layout (keep)

```text
apps/backend-adonis/
├── app/                 # domain logic
│   ├── controllers/
│   ├── exceptions/
│   ├── mails/
│   ├── middleware/
│   ├── models/
│   ├── services/        # business logic (inject into controllers)
│   ├── transformers/    # public JSON shape
│   └── validators/
├── bin/                 # server / console / test entrypoints
├── config/              # app + package config
├── database/            # migrations, schema.ts, schema_rules.ts, seeders, factories
├── providers/
├── start/               # env, kernel, routes, validators boot
├── tests/               # unit / functional + bootstrap.ts (Japa)
├── ace.js
├── adonisrc.ts
└── package.json
```

- Prefer adding folders **under `app/`** when organizing domain code (official guidance).
- Do **not** invent Nest-style `src/modules/<domain>/` or `src/common/` here.
- Commit `.adonisjs/` (generated client/server types); required for `#generated/*` and CI.
- Ignore `tmp/` (and do not ship sqlite files under `tmp/`).

## Official naming (Ace generators)

Use **`node ace make:*`** so names stay consistent with the framework.

| Artifact | File | Class / export | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Controller | `posts_controller.ts` (plural + `_controller`) | `PostsController` | `make:controller posts`; thin — no business body |
| Service | `post_service.ts` (singular + `_service`) | `PostService` | `make:service post`; business logic + `@inject` |
| Transformer | `post_transformer.ts` | `PostTransformer` | `make:transformer post`; JSON shape only |
| Middleware | `body_parser_middleware.ts` (singular + `_middleware`) | `BodyParserMiddleware` | `make:middleware` |
| Model | `user.ts` / `post.ts` (singular) | `User` / `Post` | `make:model Post`; table `posts` via Lucid |
| Validator | `user.ts` / `post.ts` (singular, by resource) | exported Vine schemas | `make:validator`; one file may hold create/update |
| Provider | `app_provider.ts` (snake_case) | — | `make:provider` |
| Migration | `*_create_posts_table.ts` | — | `make:migration` / `make:model -m` |
| DB columns | `snake_case` in SQL | `camelCase` on models | Lucid maps automatically |

**Do not** rename to Nest `auth.controller.ts` / kebab `mail-cooldown.service.ts` inside this app.

Subpath imports use package `#` aliases (`#controllers/*`, `#services/*`, `#transformers/*`, `#models/*`, …) as defined in `package.json` `imports` — not `@/`.

## Stack (this app)

| Concern | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP / DI / lifecycle | `@adonisjs/core` |
| ORM | Lucid (`@adonisjs/lucid`) — schema lives under `database/` |
| Auth | `@adonisjs/auth` **`web` session** guard |
| Mail | `@adonisjs/mail` (Resend) + Edge/`BaseMail` |
| Validation | VineJS |
| Redis | `@adonisjs/redis` |
| Cross-app policy | `@elynd/shared/auth/policy` (re-exported from `#auth/policy`) |
| Tests | Japa |
| Env | `start/env.ts` (`Env.create`) |

Persistence for **this** app is Lucid — do not introduce a second ORM package for Adonis tables.

## Env (Compose-aligned)

Validate in `start/env.ts`. Typical local Compose mapping:

- Postgres host port **5433** → `DB_HOST` / `DB_PORT` / `DB_USER` / `DB_PASSWORD` / `DB_DATABASE` (e.g. `elynd_backend`)
- Redis host port **6380** → `REDIS_HOST` / `REDIS_PORT`

## Layering (Controller / Service / Transformer)

Practical Adonis structure only — **no** Repository / UseCase / DTO towers.

Aligned with official docs: [Controllers DI](https://docs.adonisjs.com/guides/basics/controllers), [Dependency injection](https://docs.adonisjs.com/guides/concepts/dependency-injection), [`make:service`](https://docs.adonisjs.com/reference/commands) (services encapsulate business logic), [Transformers](https://docs.adonisjs.com/guides/frontend/transformers).

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Controller** | `validateUsing`; read `auth` / `params` / `request`; call **injected** services; Bouncer `authorize` when needed; return `serialize(Transformer)` / redirect | Lucid query/write; mail / token / cooldown; role defaults; frontend URL building; `new XxxService()` |
| **Service** (`app/services`) | Use-case / business rules; orchestrate Lucid, Redis, mail, encryption; throw `Exception`s | Parse raw HTTP; Vine schemas; response envelope details |
| **Transformer** | Model → public JSON (`pick`, nest, `allows` → `can.*`) | Side effects; business decisions |

- App services: `@inject()` constructor (preferred) or method injection. Framework singletons (`mail`, `redis`, …) may use `@adonisjs/.../services/...` **inside** services.
- Create a service when there is **business / use-case orchestration** — **even for a single controller** (do not wait for “2+ call sites”). Overrides always-on `structure` “1 consumer → inline” **only** for that orchestration layer. Do **not** add extra service/modules for env reads, one-call helpers, or logic that belongs as a private method on the orchestrating service.
- Validators stay Vine modules; validation runs in the controller, then trust the payload.

### Auth mail tokens (opaque Redis)

Email verification / password reset tokens are **app Redis keys** (`auth:token:{purpose}:{tokenId}` + TTL + delete on consume) — not `@adonisjs/auth` access tokens, not Plus Persona, and **no** SQL token table. Session revocation after reset uses Redis session store + tagging (`SESSION_DRIVER=redis`). Login brute-force uses `@adonisjs/limiter` `penalize`.

## Routes & HTTP

- Register routes in `start/routes.ts`; middleware stacks in `start/kernel.ts`.
- API JSON shaping: keep starter `providers/api_provider.ts` serialize wrap unless product changes the contract.

## Scaffolding

```bash
node ace make:controller posts
node ace make:service post
node ace make:transformer post
node ace make:model Post -m
node ace make:validator user
node ace make:middleware guest
node ace make:provider app
```

Prefer Ace over hand-creating differently named files.

